/*
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Nextflow config file for real, full-scale proteomes
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    conf/base.config's per-process time AND memory budgets are sized for the tiny
    4-sequence test subsample, not a real, full-size proteome -- slow steps like
    InterProScan or SignalP6 can need much longer on real data and would otherwise be
    killed for running "too long" and retried into the same wall, failing the run.
    DeepCoil2, DeepLoc2, SignalP6 and DeepTMHMM each run as a *single* task against the
    entire input FASTA (no chunking -- see workflows/rgaprofiler.nf), so their memory
    footprint scales with the real proteome's sequence count, not the test subsample's.

    No config editing needed: just add `long_running` to your -profile list, e.g.
        nextflow run . -profile docker,long_running ...
        nextflow run . -profile docker,test_full,long_running ...

    If a single week still isn't enough for your data, or a task still gets OOM-killed
    (exit code 137) even after conf/base.config's automatic retry-with-doubled-memory,
    copy this file, raise the numbers below, and point at your copy with -c instead (see
    ORIENTATIONS.md). The memory values here are a best-effort headroom bump, not a
    measured ceiling -- this pipeline has not yet been run against a full-scale (~300k
    sequence) proteome end to end (see ORIENTATIONS.md §1), so watch actual peak_rss
    per task with `-with-trace` on your first real run and adjust if needed.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*/

process {
    withLabel:process_single      { time = { 1.d  * task.attempt } }
    withLabel:process_low         { time = { 2.d  * task.attempt }; memory = { 24.GB  * task.attempt } }
    // process_medium is what DeepCoil2/DeepLoc2/SignalP6/DeepTMHMM (each running once
    // against the whole proteome) and rga_classify actually use. Sized against this
    // pipeline's own dev host (503GB RAM) on the assumption that conf/base.config's
    // process_gpu cpus lock keeps at most one of the four GPU tools active at a time --
    // if you're on a smaller machine, lower this (and prefer `--use_gpu false`, which
    // also relaxes that lock, if you need several of them to run concurrently instead).
    withLabel:process_medium      { time = { 4.d  * task.attempt }; memory = { 150.GB * task.attempt } }
    withLabel:process_high        { time = { 7.d  * task.attempt }; memory = { 100.GB * task.attempt } }
    withLabel:process_long        { time = { 10.d * task.attempt } }
}
